# UI conventions

- Read root `AGENTS.md` and `.github/instructions/ui.instructions.md`; the latter defines the shared token, brand, compact-density, and shell baseline. Consult installed Next.js documentation for framework changes.
- Use existing semantic tokens from `apps/ui/app/globals.css`; keep the sage/teal accent restrained and structural surfaces neutral. Do not hardcode component colors.
- Preserve compact, full-width operational views without shrinking interactive targets, weakening focus visibility, or relying on color alone for state.
- Reuse `components/shell/app-shell-client.tsx` and `components/shell/nav-config.tsx`; do not create another shell or duplicate global navigation.
- Keep routes in App Router pages, product components in `components/`, primitives in `components/ui/`, and requests in `lib/api-client.ts`. Prefer server components and isolate client state to interactions.
- Keep product copy direct and operational in Mozambican Portuguese (`pt-MZ`). Localize labels without changing stable API values; avoid internal acronyms, implementation details, and legal citations in product copy.
- Load the matching UI, UX, React, composition, and review skills listed in root `AGENTS.md` automatically. They inform the work but do not override the Complyz baseline or user brief.
- Coordinate UI contract changes with `packages/api-clients`, `lib/types.ts`, `lib/api-client.ts`, and contract tests.
